[%# Agent x model cost-effectiveness + output quality (admin only) — included
  # from ai/usage.tt. Data: UsageMonitor->agent_effectiveness via ledger_summary
  # (DBIx::Class group_by, no raw SQL).
  #
  # Answers the two questions a model-switch decision needs:
  #   1. What did we GET for the money — success rate, grounded rate, and
  #      flagged (uncited/hallucinated) sentences per call, per agent x model.
  #   2. Which combinations WASTE time and money — ranked by cost_wasted (spend
  #      that bought a failed call), each with a stated reason.
  #
  # No JS, no CDNs. %]
[% lm = ledger_monitor %]
[% ae = lm.agent_effectiveness %]
<div id="agent-effectiveness" class="card" style="margin:16px 0;">
  <div class="card-header">Agent cost-effectiveness &amp; output quality (admin) — last [% ae.days %] days</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    [% FOREACH e IN ae.errors %]<div class="doc-warning" role="alert">[% e | html %]</div>[% END %]

    [% IF !ae.by_agent.size %]
      <p class="doc-muted">No AI calls recorded in this window.</p>
    [% ELSE %]

      <h4>Wasting time and money</h4>
      [% IF ae.worst.size %]
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Verdict</th><th>Agent</th><th>Model</th>
              <th style="text-align:right;">Calls</th>
              <th style="text-align:right;">OK&nbsp;%</th>
              <th style="text-align:right;">$/OK</th>
              <th style="text-align:right;">Wasted&nbsp;$</th>
              <th style="text-align:right;">Flagged/call</th>
              <th>Why</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            [% FOREACH w IN ae.worst %]
              <tr>
                <td>
                  [% IF w.verdict == 'replace' %]
                    <strong style="color:var(--error-color, var(--primary-color));">replace</strong>
                  [% ELSE %]
                    <strong style="color:var(--warning-color, var(--primary-color));">watch</strong>
                  [% END %]
                </td>
                <td><code>[% w.agent | html %]</code></td>
                <td><code>[% w.provider | html %]/[% w.model | html %]</code></td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% w.calls %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% w.ok_rate %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF w.cost_per_ok.defined %][% w.cost_per_ok %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;"><strong>[% w.cost_wasted %]</strong></td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF w.flagged_per_call.defined %][% w.flagged_per_call %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
                <td class="doc-muted">[% w.why | html %]</td>
              </tr>
            [% END %]
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="doc-muted">
          <strong>Wasted&nbsp;$</strong> is real spend that bought a failed call — a failure still burns
          tokens, so this is money spent for nothing, not a score.
          Verdict rule: <em>replace</em> when fewer than 80% of calls succeeded or 0.50+ uncited
          sentences were flagged per call; <em>watch</em> below 95% or 0.01+ flagged per call.
          Pairings with fewer than 10 calls are not judged.
        </p>
      [% ELSE %]
        <p class="doc-muted">No pairing met the evidence threshold for a call-out in this window.</p>
      [% END %]

      <h4 style="margin-top:18px;">Every agent &times; model</h4>
      <p class="doc-muted">
        <strong>$/OK</strong> = money per <em>successful</em> call. A cheap model that fails half its
        calls is worse than a dear one that works, and raw totals hide that.
        <strong>Flagged/call</strong> = uncited factual sentences stripped by the grounding
        post-check — a hallucination rate.
        Agent column is grouped by <code>[% ae.source | html %]</code>[% IF ae.source == 'request_type' %]
        (the Ledger <code>feature</code> column is not in the DB yet; it appears once schema-compare
        adds it)[% END %][% IF ae.quality_source == 'none' %]; no grounding data recorded yet, so
        quality columns are blank[% ELSIF ae.quality_source %] (quality from <code>[% ae.quality_source | html %]</code>)[% END %].
      </p>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Agent</th><th>Model</th><th>Verdict</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">Calls</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">OK&nbsp;%</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">Grounded&nbsp;%</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">Flagged/call</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">Cost&nbsp;$</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">$/OK</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">Wasted&nbsp;$</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">Avg&nbsp;ms</th>
            <th style="text-align:right;">Avg&nbsp;tok</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          [% FOREACH a IN ae.by_agent %]
            [% FOREACH m IN a.models %]
              <tr>
                <td>[% IF loop.first %]<code>[% a.agent | html %]</code>[% END %]</td>
                <td><code>[% m.provider | html %]/[% m.model | html %]</code></td>
                <td>
                  [% IF m.verdict == 'replace' %]<strong style="color:var(--error-color, var(--primary-color));">replace</strong>
                  [% ELSIF m.verdict == 'watch' %]<strong style="color:var(--warning-color, var(--primary-color));">watch</strong>
                  [% ELSIF m.verdict == 'keep' %]<span style="color:var(--success-color, var(--primary-color));">keep</span>
                  [% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">unknown</span>[% END %]
                </td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% m.calls %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% m.ok_rate %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF m.grounded_rate.defined %][% m.grounded_rate %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF m.flagged_per_call.defined %][% m.flagged_per_call %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% m.cost %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF m.cost_per_ok.defined %][% m.cost_per_ok %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% m.cost_wasted %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF m.avg_ms.defined %][% m.avg_ms %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
                <td style="text-align:right;">[% m.avg_tokens %]</td>
              </tr>
            [% END %]
            <tr style="font-weight:600;border-top:2px solid var(--border-color);">
              <td colspan="3">[% a.agent | html %] — all models</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% a.calls %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% a.ok_rate %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF a.grounded_rate.defined %][% a.grounded_rate %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF a.flagged_per_call.defined %][% a.flagged_per_call %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% a.cost %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF a.cost_per_ok.defined %][% a.cost_per_ok %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% a.cost_wasted %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF a.avg_ms.defined %][% a.avg_ms %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
              <td style="text-align:right;">[% a.avg_tokens %]</td>
            </tr>
          [% END %]
          <tr style="font-weight:600;border-top:2px solid var(--primary-color);">
            <td colspan="3">All agents</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% ae.totals.calls %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% ae.totals.ok_rate %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF ae.totals.grounded_rate.defined %][% ae.totals.grounded_rate %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF ae.totals.flagged_per_call.defined %][% ae.totals.flagged_per_call %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% ae.totals.cost %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF ae.totals.cost_per_ok.defined %][% ae.totals.cost_per_ok %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% ae.totals.cost_wasted %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% IF ae.totals.avg_ms.defined %][% ae.totals.avg_ms %][% ELSE %]<span class="doc-muted">—</span>[% END %]</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;">[% ae.totals.avg_tokens %]</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p class="doc-muted">
        Model handoffs (one model failing over to another) are tracked separately in the ledger's
        <em>combinations</em> table. What a model actually <em>did</em> — the task it was given and
        whether the output was accepted — is not recorded per call anywhere yet; that needs the
        outcome scoring that posts to <a href="[% c.uri_for('/ai/eval') %]">/ai/eval</a>.
      </p>
    [% END %]
  </div>
</div>